from write_support import *
from collections import Counter
class Search:
 def __init__(self,n):self.n=n;self.rows=[];self.groups=[]
 def add(self,method,question,values,direction='CONSTRUCTIVE',use='BOTH',orientation='EXTEND',confidence='LOW',impact='MED'):
  vals=[v.strip() for v in values.split(';') if v.strip()]
  ids=[]
  for v in vals:
   id=f'G{len(self.rows)+1:03}'
   self.rows.append({'id':id,'question':question,'guess':v,'derivation':method,'direction':direction,'use':use,'orientation':orientation,'confidence':confidence,'impact':impact})
   ids.append(id)
  self.groups.append({'method':method,'count':len(vals),'first':ids[0],'last':ids[-1]})
 def output(self,input_text,parent,claims,selected,tail):
  r=self.rows
  (D/f'gg-{self.n:02}-guesses.json').write_text(json.dumps({'exact_input':input_text,'space_map':parent,'guesses':r,'selected':selected},indent=2))
  body='EXACT INPUT: '+input_text+'\n\nSPACE MAP: '+parent+'. Interpretation 2, generate possibilities. Mode BOUNDARY: the parent’s declared grid is enormous and includes incoherent cells; this execution covers boundary mechanisms rather than claiming the whole product space.\n\nLibrary check: the exact original archive was inventoried and contains no scripts/guess_library.py or guess-library dataset. No cached library was available through that source. Full generation is used and its reusable output is saved beside this document; no invocation of the absent add/lookup helpers is claimed.\n\nNon-guesses: “Find changes” is an instruction, executed here. Original source text and declared input constraints remain givens; possible representation/control designs below are candidates, not established effects.\n\nSurface claims, depth decisions and inversions:\n\n'+table(['Claim','Impact/confidence/depth','Assume right consequence','Same-scope wrong state/alternative'],claims)+'\n\nGenerated guesses. Each row answers exactly its displayed question. Derivation and all three polarity tags are explicit. Repeated meanings imported from the parent remain context; the new candidate rows vary an operation, representation, scope or boundary rather than importing a verdict.\n\n'+table(['ID','Question','Guess','Derivation','Polarity','Confidence/impact'],[[g['id'],g['question'],g['guess'],'[D: '+g['derivation']+']',f"[DIR: {g['direction']}] [USE: {g['use']}] [ORIENT: {g['orientation']}]",g['confidence']+'/'+g['impact']] for g in r])+'\n\nCoverage register:\n\n'+table(['Search method/category','Count','IDs'],[[g['method'],g['count'],g['first']+'–'+g['last']] for g in self.groups])+'\n\nAll ten morphological dimensions plus constraints are covered; seven SCAMPER operations each have four variations; twelve stakeholder perspectives and twelve explicit horizons; eight claim types each four candidates; ten analogy domains each four structural transfers; fifteen error types each two distinct failures. Inversion coverage is 100% of the listed surface claims. The question-containing input is not treated as a set of hundreds of asserted psychological facts. Analogy candidates are design constructions, not claims that a scientific mechanism empirically transfers.\n\nSpace created: actor/endorsement, representation fields, access path, timing/control and failure boundaries are explicit. Space covered: all declared search categories used, not every nominal Cartesian cell. No scientifically grounded weighting exists for an “overall percent” of the enormous possibility space; categorical completion is 100%, global-space coverage is unknown.\n\nGaps: human experience, long-term behavior, unavailable future host actions and empirical causal transfer remain unobserved. These are preserved unknown targets, not guessed outcomes. Unsupported physical interventions and concealed persuasion are excluded from current execution.\n\nConfidence × impact: all proposed effects start LOW confidence; impact distinguishes redesign-level uncertainty from a local formatting detail. High-impact candidates in the selected set receive QAG attention. Low-impact display choices are retained but not allowed to displace critical tests.\n\nSelected top twenty, separated during selection by constructive, skeptical and diagnostic pools before merging: '+', '.join(selected)+'. Selection includes output-producing candidates and EXTEND, REDIRECT and NEUTRAL orientations.\n\n'+tail
  counts={k:dict(Counter(x[k] for x in r)) for k in ['direction','use','orientation']}
  body+='\n\nPolarity totals: '+json.dumps(counts)+f'. Total guesses: {len(r)}. Constructive share: {sum(g["direction"]=="CONSTRUCTIVE" for g in r)/len(r):.1%}.\n\nRequired subordinate invocation: /qag on the critical selected guesses, recorded separately as gg-'+f'{self.n:02}'+'-qag.md. An unfinished subordinate route prevents full-completion credit.'
  record(f'gg-{self.n:02}','Open new available operations from the exact SPD target while retaining its scope boundaries.','The parent space map contains promising axes and already distinguishes source/effect or saved/triggered state. Those imported distinctions are not new mind changes here.',body,'The candidate inventory is now broader and concrete. Selection alone has not yet established benefit or transfer.','A reusable search product exists. Any new KEEP depends on subsequent executed candidates and the completed QAG route; inherited distinctions earn no credit.','UNRESOLVED','Group-specific derivations and a top-twenty selection preserve access without forcing the reader through every guess. Exact source and selected IDs remain linked.', 'Complete QAG and its route; perform a constructive candidate; check the strongest no-change boundary.',depth=f'Original GG minimum 200+ guesses and category floors. Actual {len(r)} guesses; all listed category minima met. GG has no separate numerical 8x multiplier. Parent BOUNDARY mode is retained without treating it as permission to skip the source minimum.',status='awaiting_dependency')
